  "description": "RoomBridge object catalog (protocol v1). Every client builds each kind from these parts, so the phone, Blender and the browser show the same shape. Parts live in a unit box in canonical local axes (+Y up, +Z front): x and z in [-0.5, 0.5]; y in [0, 1] for origin 'bottom', in [-0.5, 0.5] for origin 'center'. Each part is then scaled by the object's dimensions. Shapes: box; cylinder (axis +Y, may be elliptical); sphere (may be an ellipsoid). Tints: 'base' (object colour), 'dark' (base x 0.55), 'light' (base mixed 50% with white) or a fixed '#rrggbb'. 'mount' says where a novice places it from the phone: on the floor, or against a wall (facing out). 'height' is the default height of the origin above the floor.",
